{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unlit-droopy-siskin","creation_channel":"cli","description":"`bridge preview` replaces `--mode reconcile-check` and `--mode dry-run`. A design spike established\nthese are NOT a shared intermediate — they share only `fetcher.compute_snapshot`, the binding store,\nand the `classify` module, and diverge on everything downstream:\n\n- Local set: reconcile-check reads every `.cache.json` dir including archived/deleted; dry-run runs\n  `rebar list --full` (active only).\n- Field comparison: reconcile-check uses `_compare_pair`, UNARBITRATED — any difference is a\n  discrepancy. Dry-run uses `outbound_field_diff`, arbitrated against the per-binding baseline\n  (ADR 0026) with directionality suppression and local-wins.\n- Neither output is derivable from the other. A reconcile-check discrepancy can produce NO mutation\n  (baseline says local is unchanged); a dry-run mutation can exist with NO discrepancy (ADOPT of an\n  unbound issue, TERMINAL_TRANSITION for an archived ticket — both invisible to the bound-pair loop).\n\n`_compare_pair` is the differ's comparison re-implemented by hand, and its own comments prove it is\nchasing the original: \"must match the differ's exclusion set exactly\", \"canonicalized the same way\n625b canonicalized the outbound differ\". It already imports `_assignee_matches` from the differ.\n\nRecommendation: ONE verb, ONE pass, two sections — `{plan, drift}` — because two verbs would run the\nexpensive Jira fetch twice. But the merge is real work, not a rename: the field detail must come\nfrom the differ (surface `outbound_field_diff`'s existing `changed` dict on the plan entry) and\n`_compare_pair` must be DELETED, or you have shipped two computations behind one verb.\n\n**Also: preview must take no lock.** Today `dry-run` runs the full lock ceremony including\n`_purge_committed_reconciler_locks` (a git CAS commit) and can STEAL A LIVE PASS'S LEASE to run a\nread-only preview.\n\n**Two bugs folded in.** `docs/user-guide.md:364` documents `rebar reconcile --dry-run`, which does\nnot exist — argparse's `allow_abbrev` resolves it to `--dry-run-enumerate`, so it prints ticket\ndirectory paths and exits 0 WITHOUT reconciling, looking exactly like a successful dry run.\nReproduced. Setting `allow_abbrev=False` makes that whole error class impossible rather than fixing\none instance; a verb (not a flag) makes it unforgettable.\n\nThis ticket gates nothing else in the epic and can land independently.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `bridge preview` runs one cap-0 pass and emits both the plan and the field-level drift\n- [ ] Field detail comes from the differ; `reconcile_check._compare_pair` is deleted\n- [ ] Preview acquires no lock and never purges or steals one\n- [ ] The two local-ticket loaders are reconciled to one read\n- [ ] `allow_abbrev=False` on the parser, with a test that an abbreviated/unknown option exits 2\n- [ ] `docs/user-guide.md:364` is corrected\n- [ ] The `bridge_state/reconcile-check.json` write is dropped; preview writes stdout","id":"424f-bc35-b7ca-419a","parent_id":"2f79-2b32-28c5-4eb3","priority":2,"tags":["bridge"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Merge preview into one pass and make the abbreviation bug impossible"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786047582784571001,"uuid":"3f180b25-8551-4cac-8e26-4333b777f242"}